@startuml serverv2_bounded_contexts
title serverV2 -- three bounded contexts, each layered (modular monolith)\nRendering reaches Billing and Identity through PORTS (forward) and reacts to EVENTS (reverse).\nNo context imports another's domain. bootstrap.py is the ONLY place they are wired together.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam BackgroundColor white
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam classBackgroundColor #fafafa
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 22
skinparam ranksep 42

' ============================================================
' SHARED KERNEL -- everyone may depend on this; keep it TINY
' ============================================================
package "shared_kernel" as SK #e5e7eb {
  class "UserId" as UID
  class "Money / Credits" as MONEY
  interface "IEventBus" as BUS
}

' ============================================================
' RENDERING CONTEXT
' ============================================================
package "RENDERING context" as REN #dbeafe {
  package "presentation" as REN_P #eff6ff {
    class "routers/render_groups" as REN_R
  }
  package "application" as REN_A #eff6ff {
    class "HandleChunkSucceeded\nReconcileGroupStatus" as REN_UC
    class "OnCreditsExhausted\n(event handler)" as REN_EV
    interface "ICreditsService  (port)" as PORT_CS
    interface "IUserDirectory  (port)" as PORT_UD
  }
  package "domain" as REN_D #eff6ff {
    class "RenderGroup\nChunkCostRule" as REN_ENT
  }
  package "infrastructure" as REN_I #eff6ff {
    class "CreditsServiceAdapter" as ADPT_CS
    class "UserDirectoryAdapter" as ADPT_UD
    class "RenderGroupRepository" as REN_REPO
  }
}

' ============================================================
' BILLING CONTEXT
' ============================================================
package "BILLING context" as BIL #dcfce7 {
  package "presentation" as BIL_P #f0fdf4 {
    class "routers/credits" as BIL_R
  }
  package "application" as BIL_A #f0fdf4 {
    class "ChargeCredits  (public)\nGrantCredits   GetBalance" as BIL_UC
  }
  package "domain" as BIL_D #f0fdf4 {
    class "CreditBalance\nUsdToCreditsRule" as BIL_ENT
    class "CreditsExhausted\n(domain event)" as BIL_EVT
  }
  package "infrastructure" as BIL_I #f0fdf4 {
    class "LedgerRepository" as BIL_REPO
  }
}

' ============================================================
' IDENTITY CONTEXT
' ============================================================
package "IDENTITY context" as IDN #fef9c3 {
  package "presentation" as IDN_P #fefce8 {
    class "routers/users" as IDN_R
  }
  package "application" as IDN_A #fefce8 {
    class "GetUserProfile  (public)\nRegisterUser" as IDN_UC
  }
  package "domain" as IDN_D #fefce8 {
    class "User" as IDN_ENT
  }
  package "infrastructure" as IDN_I #fefce8 {
    class "UserRepository" as IDN_REPO
  }
}

' ============================================================
' COMPOSITION ROOT
' ============================================================
class "bootstrap.py\ncomposition root" as BOOT #ffffff

' ---------- INSIDE rendering : normal layered deps, all inward ----------
REN_R --> REN_UC
REN_UC --> REN_ENT
REN_UC --> PORT_CS : (1) charge per tick
REN_UC --> PORT_UD
ADPT_CS ..|> PORT_CS : (2) implements
ADPT_UD ..|> PORT_UD
REN_REPO ..> REN_ENT

' ---------- INSIDE billing / identity : layered deps ----------
BIL_R --> BIL_UC
BIL_UC --> BIL_ENT
BIL_REPO ..> BIL_ENT
IDN_R --> IDN_UC
IDN_UC --> IDN_ENT
IDN_REPO ..> IDN_ENT

' ---------- CROSS-CONTEXT : FORWARD  (rendering -> billing / identity) ----------
ADPT_CS --> BIL_UC : (3) calls billing PUBLIC use-case
ADPT_UD --> IDN_UC : calls identity PUBLIC use-case

' ---------- CROSS-CONTEXT : REVERSE  (billing -> rendering) via event, NO import ----------
BIL_EVT ..> BUS : (4) publish CreditsExhausted
BUS ..> REN_EV : (5) deliver
REN_EV --> REN_UC : (6) rendering cancels itself

' ---------- shared kernel usage ----------
REN_ENT ..> UID
BIL_ENT ..> UID
BIL_ENT ..> MONEY

' ---------- wiring (composition root) ----------
BOOT ..> ADPT_CS : binds port to adapter
BOOT ..> ADPT_UD

note as NFLOW #eef2ff
  Cross-context communication -- the whole story
  ==
  FORWARD  (rendering needs billing) = a synchronous PORT call:
  (1) a render use-case calls its OWN port, ICreditsService.charge
  (2) an adapter in rendering.infrastructure implements that port
  (3) the adapter calls billing's PUBLIC application use-case (ChargeCredits)
      -- never billing's domain or tables
  Identity works the same way through IUserDirectory.

  REVERSE  (billing affects rendering) = a decoupled EVENT:
  (4) billing publishes CreditsExhausted on the shared IEventBus
  (5) the bus delivers it to a rendering event-handler
  (6) rendering cancels the group using its OWN use-case
      -- billing never imports or calls rendering

  So the graph is ACYCLIC: forward = port, reverse = event.
  bootstrap.py is the ONLY place a port meets a concrete adapter.
end note

@enduml
